BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260831T210000Z
DTEND:20260831T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T000000Z
SUMMARY:Bricks & Beyond: A Lego Challenge Club
DESCRIPTION:Once a month\, tweens and teens take over the MakerLab for LEGO 
 chaos. Wild themes. Weird prompts. Timed builds. Robot races. You bring the 
 creativity\, we bring the bricks.\n\nWin the monthly challenge\, wow the 
 judges\, and you could win a full LEGO set!\n\nBuild big. Build weird. 
 Build to win.\n\nWe will meet on the last Monday of every month\, starting 
 at 5PM on the 1st floor Makerlab. \n\nThis program was made possible 
 through a generous donation from the Friends of Durham Library.\n\n\nUna 
 vez al mes\, preadolescentes y adolescentes toman el control del MakerLab 
 para un caos total de LEGO. Temas salvajes. Retos rarísimos. 
 Construcciones contra el reloj. Carreras de robots. Tú traes la 
 creatividad\, nosotros ponemos los bloques.\n\n¡Gana el reto mensual\, 
 sorprende a los jueces y podrías llevarte un set completo de 
 LEGO!\n\nConstruye en grande. Construye raro. Construye para ganar.\n\nNos 
 reuniremos el último lunes de cada mes\, comenzando a las 5:00 PM en el 
 MakerLab del 1er piso.\n\nEste programa fue posible gracias a una generosa 
 donación de Friends of Durham Library.
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Abigail Mondragon":MAILTO:vasmondragon@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Friends of the Durham Library
UID:LibCal-14288-16505695
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16505695
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260831T220000Z
DTEND:20260831T224500Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T000000Z
SUMMARY:Heartfulness Meditation
DESCRIPTION:Heartfulness meditation practice is a simple and effective way 
 to integrate meditation into our daily lives. The Heartfulness technique 
 shows us how to gently turn our attention toward our hearts and experience 
 that inner presence for ourselves. There will be a brief introduction and 
 instruction\, followed by a guided relaxation\, leading into a silent 
 heart-centered meditation. Sessions are conducted by a certified 
 Heartfulness meditation instructor and open to everyone over the age of 15. 
 No prior experience necessary. Registration is not required.\n\nIf you have 
 questions about accessibility\, program stimulation levels\, and/or need 
 disability accommodations\, please contact us at 919-560-8593.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carmen Ruth":MAILTO:cruth@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness, Low Sensory Stimulation
UID:LibCal-14288-16877774
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16877774
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260831T223000Z
DTEND:20260831T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260831T000000Z
SUMMARY:Gentle Yoga @ Main
DESCRIPTION:This series will take place in our outdoor amphitheater by the 
 lower parking lot (by our MakerLab entrance).\n\nNeed a break from your 
 hectic schedule?  Release the stress of your day with outdoor Gentle Yoga 
 at Main Library - Nicole Varnado\, RYT-200\, is offering this six-week 
 series of gentle flow yoga for adults on Monday evenings!  Classes are 
 accessible to all-comers\, and will include guided meditation\, 
 breathwork\, movement\, and yoga philosophy.  Please bring a yoga mat or 
 towel for class (we have a few available if you do not have one)\, and wear 
 'moveable' clothes.  If you bring a reusable water bottle\, you can refill 
 it at one of the filling stations in the library.\n\nIf class must be 
 relocated due to inclement weather\, registrants will be notified by 
 email.\n\n
LOCATION:Main Library - Outdoors - Amphitheatre\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness
