DTEND:20260904T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260904T000000Z
SUMMARY:Restorative Yoga
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin us for a 50-minute class for adults that will provide an 
 opportunity for you to relax through gentle stretching and mindful 
 breathing. This class is designed for anyone who would like to slow down\, 
 connect with the body and calm the mind. Both beginners and experienced 
 yogis are welcome. During the class\, you will be guided through a series 
 of yoga poses and mindful breathing techniques intended to calm the busy 
 mind and stretch the body.\n\nPlease bring a yoga mat or towel to the 
 program. Space is limited. Registration is required.\n\nIf you have 
 questions about accessibility and/or need accommodations\, please contact 
 Mara (she/her): mplantholt@dconc.gov or 919-560-0207.\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout the 
 presenter: \n\nCatherine Gupta trained in MindBody Centering Yoga in 2018. 
 Her teaching style blends humor lightness with a focus on calming and 
 supporting the nervous system. She has called Durham home since 2012 and is 
 the author of two books: The Manor She Left Behind and The Unexpected 
 Connection. She is passionate about creating spaces that foster meaningful 
 connection and a sense of belonging.\n\n\n \n
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-16798666
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16798666
END:VEVENT
