SUMMARY:Fall Clothing Swap with Circular Triangle and Durham Mother's Club
DESCRIPTION:Refresh you and your child’s wardrobe and toy shelf without 
 spending a dime! Join us for a community Clothing & Toy Swap\, organized by 
 the Durham Mothers Club and Circular Triangle. \n\n\n	Please limit 
 contributions to two bags. \n	You are not required to bring an item to 
 participate in the swap (there are always leftovers)\, so feel free to stop 
 by and take an item or two. \n	Registration is not required - please feel 
 free to stop in any time between 10am-12pm\n\n\nAbout Circular 
 Triangle:\n\nCircular Triangle aims to raise awareness about the waste 
 hierarchy and promote circular alternatives\, particularly in textiles. We 
 foster education and advocacy on the intersection of municipal systems and 
 circular economy principles\, while providing a connection hub to support 
 organizations dedicated to these sustainable solutions.\n\n\n \n\nAbout 
 Durham Mother's Club: \n\n\n\nThe Durham Mothers Club is a support network 
 for all moms in Durham\, North Carolina and surrounding communities.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16563555
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16563555
END:VEVENT
