SUMMARY:Journey to Antarctica!
DESCRIPTION:Penguins! Parkas! Phenomenal science! Join us in the Innovation 
 Lab (3rd floor) at Main Library for a presentation and discussion with 
 Margaret Milikin\, a logistics expert who works at McMurdo Station in 
 Antarctica. Learn about Antarctica's wildlife\, life at McMurdo\, and what 
 type of career path could lead YOU to this icy paradise. \n\nRegistration 
 is required. We recommend this program for tweens (ages 9-12)\, teens\, and 
 adults. \n\nThis event will open to waitlisted registrants at 6:15pm\, at 
 which time seating will be first come\, first served. \n\nPlease note\, 
 parking may be limited due to other library programming. If needed\, you 
 may park in the Queen Street Parking Deck (115 N. Queen St.) and the 
 Library will validate your ticket.\n\nIf you have any accessibility 
 questions or accommodation needs\, please contact Jennifer at 
 Accessibility_Services@dconc.gov. We ask that\, if possible\, all 
 accommodation requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to 
 the event.
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Accessibility Services":MAILTO:accessibility_services@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, High Sensory Stimulation, STEAM
