DTSTAMP:20260909T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: Wild Dark Shore
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte McConaghy. The description for the book is 
 below:\n"Dominic Salt and his three children are caretakers of Shearwater\, 
 a tiny island not far from Antarctica. Home to the world's largest seed 
 bank\, Shearwater was once full of researchers\, but with sea levels 
 rising\, the Salts are now its final inhabitants. Until\, during the worst 
 storm the island has ever seen\, a woman mysteriously washes ashore. 
 Isolation has taken its toll on the Salts\, but as they nurse the woman\, 
 Rowan\, back to strength\, it begins to feel like she might just be what 
 they need.\n\nRowan\, long accustomed to protecting herself\, starts 
 imagining a future where she could belong to someone again. But Rowan isn't 
 telling the whole truth about why she set out for Shearwater. And when she 
 discovers sabotaged radios and a freshly dug grave\, she realizes Dominic 
 is keeping his own secrets. As the storms on Shearwater gather force\, they 
 all must decide if they can trust one another enough to protect the 
 precious seeds in their care before it's too late--and if they can finally 
 put the tragedies of the past behind them to create something new\, 
 together."\n\nWe look forward to seeing you all soon!\n\n\nInterested in 
 attending a future Daytime Book Club meeting? Take a look at our reading 
 list below:\n\nMay 2026: To the Lighthouse by Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: 
 The Night Watchman by Louise Erdrich\n\nJuly 2026: A Marriage at Sea by 
 Sophie Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: My Friends by Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 
 2026: Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on 
 Mango Street by Sandra Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of 
 Good and Evil by John Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha 
 Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: 
 Song of Solomon by Toni Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli 
 Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576146
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576146
