SUMMARY:Bite into Science
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive series to discover the exciting 
 world of nutrition\, healthy habits\, and food science! Through hands-on 
 experiments\, engaging demonstrations\, games\, and creative activities\, 
 kids will learn how their bodies use food for energy\, why healthy choices 
 matter\, and how science is all around us. Each session is designed to 
 spark curiosity\, encourage healthy lifestyles\, and make learning fun. No 
 prior science experience is needed—just bring your curiosity and get 
 ready to explore!\n\nAbout the presenters: Sophie and Yoojin are Duke 
 undergraduate students interested in pursuing careers in medicine who are 
 passionate about promoting nutrition and wellness through early education. 
 They enjoy making science fun while inspiring young learners to build 
 healthy habits that can last a lifetime.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Main Library":MAILTO:main@durhamcountylibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
