SUMMARY:Page & Pen Writing Workshop -- Writing Prompts Extravaganza
DESCRIPTION:\n\nGrab your notebook and a pen\, and let's write! The Page & 
 Pen Writing Workshop meets roughly every six weeks and is open to anyone 
 who wants to improve their creative writing skills. Session formats vary 
 and may include writing exercises\, discussion about technique and 
 process\, sharing ideas for organizing work sessions and workspaces\, or 
 exploration of any challenges you may be facing in the struggle to 
 write.\n\n\n\nThis session: Writing Prompts Extravaganza! This will be a 
 modified reprise of the three sessions we did during summer of 2025. Prompt 
 exercises will include a Story Card Deck\, a Mix and Match scenario\, and 
 various poetry prompts. We'll also open up the floor to the group\, so if 
 you have any favorite writing prompt exercises\, feel free to bring them 
 along.\n\nThis program is open to anyone at any time: drop in once\, attend 
 every session\, or show up every once in a while -- no long-term commitment 
 is required. Space is often limited\, so please register in 
 advance.\n\nContact Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy, Writing
