DTEND:20260912T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260912T000000Z
SUMMARY:Get Ready for Observe the Moon Night (drop-in stations)
DESCRIPTION:This year's International Observe the Moon Night is Saturday\, 
 September 19th! Join the Maker   STEAM team for drop-in stations with 
 activities and resources to get ready for Observe the Moon Night with loads 
 of resources from NASA. In these stations\, you can:\n\n\n	\n	Make moon 
 art\n	\n	\n	Virtually explore the moon's surface\n	\n	\n	Act out orbiting 
 around the moon with a 3D printed model\n	\n	\n	and more!\n	\n\n\nEach of 
 these stations will be exploration and observation\, with a mix of digital 
 activities and screen-free activities. These activities are geared towards 
 ages 5 and up\, all ages welcome.\n\nRead more about Internation Observe 
 the Moon Night here - 
 https://science.nasa.gov/moon/observe-the-moon-night/. \n\nThis program is 
 drop-in\, no registration required. Please join us between 3pm and 5pm in 
 the Innovation Lab on 3rd floor of Main Library. The stations will take 
 most participants around 30 to 45 minutes in total to complete. This event 
 is for all ages\; children under age 11 must be accompanied by an adult. 
 \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please 
 contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at 
 least 3 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, High Sensory Stimulation, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-17368044
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17368044
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
SUMMARY:One Walk to Rule Them All Exercise Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Join us for One Walk to Rule Them All\, a Lord of the 
 Rings-themed exercise initiative that will inspire you to participate in 
 your favorite types of exercises! To participate\, simply pick up a printed 
 tracker from either South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave.) or North 
 Regional Library (221 Milton Rd) or click HERE to request a printable PDF 
 via email. Trackers will be available beginning August 24th.\n\nHow it 
 works: \n\n\n	You have until November 30th to complete at least four of the 
 five challenges listed on the tracker. \n	You can join in at any time 
 during September\, October\, or November!\n	You can do any type of exercise 
 or physical activity you like! \n	Use your tracker to track the number of 
 minutes you exercise.\n	For each challenge on the tracker you complete\, 
 bring your tracker in to South Regional Library or North Regional Library 
 to claim your completion button for that challenge. You will also receive a 
 lanyard upon your first visit. (while supplies last). If you prefer\, you 
 can claim them all at the end of the challenge.\n	Return your tracker to 
 South or North Regional by December 10th to be entered into the grand prize 
 raffle. \n	If you complete all five challenges on the tracker\, you earn 
 two entries.\n	You can earn extra entries into the raffle by attending 
 specific programs/events throughout September\, October and November. Click 
 HERE for a list of those programs. You must return a completed tracker to 
 be eligible to receive extra entries.\n	All ages are welcome to 
 participate\, however we do not have separate prizes for different age 
 groups. \n\n\nThere will be five winners! The Grand Prizes are: \n\n\n	Two 
 Fitbit Charges\n	Two Lord of the Rings themed gift bags filled with some 
 cool LOTR stuff. \n	One Lord of the Rings Lego set (Balrog book 
 nook)\n\n\nQuestions? Please contact Jessica at jllundin@dconc.gov\n\nOne 
 Walk to Rule Them All is made possible through the generosity of the 
 Friends of the Durham Library.\n
LOCATION:South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Friends of the Durham Library, Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-16258371
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16258371
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260913T140000Z
DTEND:20260913T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260913T000000Z
SUMMARY:Declaration of Independence: Rare Prints on Display
DESCRIPTION:\n\nWe invite you to view rare 19th-century prints of the 
 Declaration of Independence at Durham County Main Library.\n\nAs part of We 
 the People: A Duke & Durham Initiative\, Durham County Main Library and the 
 Nasher Museum of Art at Duke University are presenting three historic 
 copies of the Declaration of Independence on loan from the David M. 
 Rubenstein Americana Collection. This exhibition offers a rare opportunity 
 to explore how the nation's founding document was visually rendered and 
 circulated in early American history.\n\n\n\nThe exhibition will feature 
 three rare prints on loan from the David M. Rubenstein Americana 
 Collection: a rare official full-sized 1823 facsimile engraved by William 
 J. Stone (known as a Stone Declaration) alongside two historic broadside 
 copies from the same era: an 1818 reproduction by calligrapher Benjamin 
 Owen Tyler and a more ornate 1819 illustrated version published by John 
 Binns. \n\nVisitors can also engage with interactive activities and explore 
 featured library resources on display alongside the historic 
 prints.\n\n\n\n \n\nGallery Hours at Durham County Main 
 Library\n\nSeptember 8\, 2026 – September 20\, 2026\n\nMonday – 
 Wednesday: 10:00 AM – 7:00 PM\n\nThursday – Saturday: 10:00 AM – 5:00 
 PM\n\nSunday: 1:30 PM – 5:00 PM\n\n*Gallery entry is on the 2nd floor of 
 Main Library*\n\n\n\n \n\nGroup Visits & Planning Your 
 Entry\n\nPre-registered group visits (10  people) take place Monday – 
 Friday from 10:00 AM – 3:30 PM. Groups of 10  may sign up for self-guided 
 times here.\n\nIndividual visitors are welcome at all times\, but please 
 note you may experience a brief wait to enter if the gallery is at capacity 
 or if a large group is inside.\n\n\n\n \n\nRead With Us\n\nUS 
 Constitution/Declaration of Independence Childrens' Booklist \n\nUS 
 Constitution/Declaration of Independence Adult Booklist \n\n \n\nExhibition 
 Related Programming\n\nRedeeming the Promise of the Declaration of 
 Independence: Louis Austin\, the Black Press\, and the 20th Century Freedom 
 Struggle - Wednesday\, September 9\, 2026 at 6 p.m.\n\nHer Fight\, His 
 Name: The Story of Gwen Carr and Eric Garner - Thursday\, September 10\, 
 2026 at 6:30 p.m.\n\nThe American Revolution at 250: Historians Discuss the 
 Many Worlds of 1776 - Tuesday\, September 15\, 2026 at 6 p.m.\n\n\n\nFull 
 Durham Schedule\n\nTo maximize access across the region\, the documents are 
 hosted in two Durham spaces:\n\n\n	Durham County Main Library: September 8 
 – September 20\, 2026\n	Nasher Museum of Art at Duke University: 
 September 24\, 2026 – January 3\, 2027 - click here for more 
 information\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Declaration of Independence is organized in 
 collaboration with Duke Arts and the Nasher Museum of Art and is part of We 
 the People: A Duke & Durham Initiative that marks the 250th anniversary of 
 the signing of the Declaration of Independence through a series of public 
 events examining the nation’s evolving identity. Three historic copies of 
 the Declaration of Independence are on loan from the David M. Rubenstein 
 Americana Collection. Leadership support for We the People has been 
 generously provided by David M. Rubenstein. \n\n\nInformation on Entering 
 Main Library\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the 
 North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind 
 the apartments directly across the street from the library.
LOCATION:Main Library - Auditorium - Upper Corridor 2nd Floor\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17651809
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17651809
END:VEVENT
