SUMMARY:Trinket Stop Ribbon Cutting & Swap
DESCRIPTION:Southwest Regional Library is getting a Trinket Stop! 
 \n\nTrinket stops are free\, curated public exchanges filled with whimsical 
 “trinkets” including stickers\, keychains\, figurines\, toys\, etc. 
 They are created with the goal to bring accessible and whimsical spaces to 
 communities and to encourage community members to swap trinkets. The 
 Southwest trinket stop is sponsored by our neighbors at Regrowth 
 Counseling. \n\nJoin us for a ribbon cutting (tiny scissors may be 
 involved) and feel free to bring your own trinket to swap and share with 
 other friends!
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Outdoor Space\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-17355109
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17355109
END:VEVENT
