SUMMARY:Speech and Language Development in Children - Norms and Expected Timeframes
DESCRIPTION:Are you wondering if your child’s speech or language skills 
 are developing as expected? Would you like to know how best to support your 
 child's development in speech and language skill? \n\nCome and discover the 
 expected developmental timeframes for speech and language skills to emerge 
 for children ages birth through 7-years and how best to support growth in 
 the following areas: speech articulation skills\, receptive language\, 
 expressive language\, and social-pragmatic language. \n\nPresenter: Rebecca 
 J. Sheffield\, MS\, CCC-SLP\n\nSpeech Language Pathologist with over 20 
 years of experience working with young children
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carmen Ruth":MAILTO:cruth@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
