SUMMARY:Home Repair Lab Special Program: Energy Saving 101
DESCRIPTION:*This program has moved to Room #3214 on Main Library's 3rd 
 floor.\n\nJoin Chris and Mindy Meyers from Home Repair Lab for a special 
 program at Main Library! This Energy Saving 101 lecture will discuss the 
 whys and hows of energy savings in your home! \nParticipants will leave 
 this program with an understanding on energy consumption and waste in the 
 home\, access information about energy savings\, and ways to provide home 
 comfort while saving energy.\n\nRelevant for homeowners\, first time home 
 buyers\, and renters. The first hour will be lecture\, followed by 
 interactive Q&A. \n\n__\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 2 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Maker, STEAM
